const pw = (s) => s;
exports.q2 = () => {
  const T = d.tests;
  return [
    h1("Question 2: Requirements and Traceability"),
    h2("2.1 Final prioritised requirements"),
    p("Identifiers and priorities (MoSCoW) are those of Assignment 2. Acceptance criteria are restated so that each can be checked with a number. The Assignment 2 numbering gaps (NFR-03, NFR-04, and so on) are kept, because those requirements were never specified."),
    table(["ID", "Priority", "Requirement", "Measurable acceptance criterion"], [
      ["FR-01", "Must", "Dispatch the nearest available drone when a CAD alert arrives.", "Given a valid alert, the nearest idle drone with battery of 30% or more is assigned and marked `en_route` within 30 s."],
      ["FR-02", "Must", "Stream drone telemetry (GPS, altitude, battery, heading) to the dashboard over WebSocket.", "Dashboard receives each update within 500 ms of ingest."],
      ["FR-03", "Must", "Classify each thermal frame as No Fire, Fire or Critical.", "Result returned within 100 ms per frame."],
      ["FR-04", "Must", "Overlay detected hotspots on the GIS map during an incident.", "Hotspot event reaches the map within 2 s of detection."],
      ["FR-05", "Should", "Produce a fire-spread prediction overlay every 60 s from hotspots, weather and terrain.", "Overlay refreshes every 60 s using current hotspot, weather and terrain inputs."],
      ["FR-06", "Must", "Track all deployed firefighters by GPS on the dashboard (mobile app).", "Dashboard shows a crew position within 5 s of the update."],
      ["FR-07", "Should", "Command messaging between commanders, operators and crew.", "A sent message reaches every connected recipient in real time."],
      ["FR-08", "Must", "Mobile app usable one-handed with gloves; buttons at least 44 × 44 px.", "Gloved one-handed operation without mis-taps."],
      ["FR-09", "Should", "Automatic post-incident report with thermal image, hotspot timeline and AI analysis.", "Report available within 5 minutes of closing an incident."],
      ["FR-10", "Must", "Whole system runs on simulated drone data through the HAL.", "Dispatch, telemetry, AI analysis and reporting all work with no drone hardware."],
      ["NFR-01", "Must", "Reliability: uptime and automatic failover during incidents.", "99.5% uptime during incident handling, with automatic backend failover."],
      ["NFR-02", "Must", "Performance: dashboard load time.", "Loads within 3 s on a 10 Mbps connection."],
      ["NFR-05", "Should", "Supportability: containerised services.", "Backend runs from a Docker image on any cloud with no code change."],
      ["NFR-10", "Must", "Security: data encrypted in transit and at rest.", "TLS 1.3 in transit; AES-256 for data stored in MongoDB Atlas."],
      ["ETR-01", "Must", "CNN accuracy before deployment.", "At least 90% accuracy on the FLAME validation split."],
      ["ETR-02", "Must", "Real-time inference rate and CPU budget.", "At least 10 frames/s sustained with no more than 80% CPU."],
      ["ETR-04", "Should", "Hotspot localisation accuracy.", "Hotspots localised within 5 m when georeferenced onto the map."],
    ], [9, 9, 38, 44], { size: 16 }),
    h2("2.2 Requirements traceability matrix"),
    p("Test cases are defined in Section 5.1 (UT = unit, IT = integration, ST = system). UML references point to the figures in Section 3 (UC = use case in Figure 2). Status is **Pass**, **Partial** or **Not met**, judged against the acceptance criterion above, not against a relaxed version of it."),
    table(["Req.", "UML reference", "Module", "Test case", "Status"], [
      ["FR-01", "UC-02, Fig. 2, 4, 5a", "`app.main` dispatch(), nearest_available_drone()", "IT-02, IT-04, ST-01", ["Pass"]],
      ["FR-02", "UC-03, Fig. 4", "`app.main` ingest_telemetry(), Hub", "IT-05, ST-01", ["Pass"]],
      ["FR-03", "UC-04, Fig. 4", "`app.ai.engine` AIEngine.analyse()", "UT-06, IT-06, ST-01", ["Pass"]],
      ["FR-04", "UC-05, Fig. 4", "`hotspots` event, `app.static/app.js`", "IT-06, ST-01, UI capture", ["Pass"]],
      ["FR-05", "UC-06, Fig. 6", "`app.spread` predict(); 60 s timer in `app.js`", "UT-08, IT-10", ["Partial"]],
      ["FR-06", "UC-07, Fig. 3", "`/firefighters/{id}/location`, Hub", "IT-07", ["Partial"]],
      ["FR-07", "UC-08, Fig. 3", "`/messages`, Hub", "IT-08", ["Pass"]],
      ["FR-08", "None (no mobile client)", "Not implemented", "None", ["Not met"]],
      ["FR-09", "UC-09, UC-10, Fig. 3", "`app.report` build_report()", "IT-09, ST-01", ["Pass"]],
      ["FR-10", "Fig. 3, 6 (DroneAdapter)", "`app.hal` SimulatedDrone, FireScenario", "UT-09, IT-11, ST-01", ["Pass"]],
      ["NFR-01", "Fig. 7 (deployment)", "None (single process, no failover)", "None", ["Not met"]],
      ["NFR-02", "Fig. 7", "`app.static` (index.html, app.js)", "UI capture (5 cold loads)", ["Pass"]],
      ["NFR-05", "Fig. 7", "`Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml`", "Not run (no Docker daemon)", ["Partial"]],
      ["NFR-10", "Fig. 7", "`app.security`; TLS at server/gateway", "UT-01, UT-02, ST-02", ["Partial"]],
      ["ETR-01", "Fig. 1, 4", "`app.ai.train`, `app.ai.model`", "UT-06, training run", ["Partial"]],
      ["ETR-02", "Fig. 4, 7", "`app.ai.engine`, mission loop", "ST-01", ["Partial"]],
      ["ETR-04", "Fig. 4", "`app.ai.engine` hotspots(), `app.geo`", "UT-07, UT-04, sweep", ["Partial"]],
    ], [8, 20, 31, 23, 10], { statusCol: 4, size: 16 }),
    spacer(60),
    p(`**Summary of the 17 requirements: 8 Pass, 7 Partial, 2 Not met.** Not met: FR-08 (no mobile app) and NFR-01 (no uptime measurement or failover exists). Partial results are explained in Section 2.3 and Section 5.2. On FR-04: the hotspot event is broadcast in the same processing step as the detection (inference p95 ${d.sys.inference_ms.p95} ms), so it reaches the browser well inside 2 s; the browser drawing time itself was not instrumented.`),
    h2("2.3 How the emerging-technology requirements are satisfied"),
    h3("ETR-01: CNN accuracy of at least 90% on the FLAME validation split (Partial)"),
    p(`The CNN (${d.ai.parameters.toLocaleString()} parameters, 3 convolution blocks and a 3-class head) reaches **${(d.ai.val_accuracy * 100).toFixed(2)}%** accuracy on a held-out validation set of ${d.ai.val_samples.toLocaleString()} frames, and 90% or more on 450 freshly generated frames in UT-06. **This is not the FLAME dataset.** FLAME could not be downloaded in the build environment, so the model was trained and validated on synthetic thermal frames that include warm-roof distractors and overlapping class sizes. The number shows the pipeline works and that the model separates the three classes on this data. It does not show real-world accuracy, and the requirement as written is therefore only partly satisfied. Retraining on FLAME plus locally captured footage is the first future improvement (Section 5.4).`),
    h3("ETR-02: 10 frames per second within an 80% CPU budget (Partial)"),
    p(`A live server test streamed thermal frames for 15 s on scene at **${d.f1(d.sys.frame_rate_fps)} frames/s** (${d.sys.detections} frames analysed over the whole run). Inference took a median of ${d.sys.inference_ms.p50} ms and a p95 of ${d.sys.inference_ms.p95} ms per frame, and the server used about **${d.f1(d.sys.server_cpu_percent_of_one_core)}% of one core** on a ${d.sys.cpu_cores_available}-core machine, far below the 80% ceiling. The requirement names an Azure App Service instance, which was not available, so the result is Partial. An earlier version of the mission loop slept a fixed 100 ms after each frame and reached only 9.43 frames/s. This was fixed with a fixed-rate schedule and re-measured.`),
    h3("ETR-04: hotspots localised within 5 m (Partial)"),
    p(`Hotspots are found by thresholding the frame, labelling connected components and projecting each component centroid to latitude and longitude with a nadir-camera model (60° field of view, drone GPS, altitude and heading). Against the simulator's known fire positions, a sweep over 4 fires, 3 altitudes (60, 80, 100 m) and 30 time steps produced ${d.geo.n} hotspot detections: median error **${d.geo.p50} m**, 95th percentile **${d.geo.p95} m**, and **${d.geo.within} of ${d.geo.n} (${d.geo.pct}%)** within 5 m. Two detections exceeded 5 m (worst ${d.geo.max} m), both in Critical frames where a large blob was merged or clipped at the frame edge. Because the requirement says "within 5 metres" without a percentile, and the ground truth is simulated (real GPS and camera error are not included), the status is Partial.`),
  ];
};
